  nonce: 6b30  # 6b30
  message: "UNBLOCKED BY THE OWNER'S BAND RULING, 2026-08-30. Recorded here because this\nitem was gated by a rule that no longer exists, and the next reader would\notherwise re-derive the gate from LIVE/AGENTS text written while it held.\n\nWI-sivuz's \"<50% => recall work should stop\" is retired as an automatic gate.\nThe replacement test is by MECHANISM: accuracy work is always in; new-surface\nwork carries its own precision estimate.\n\nTHIS ITEM IS ON THE ACCURACY SIDE, and measurably so rather than by argument.\nIts own census of 236 bufio.NewScanner/NewReader call sites:\n\n    153 (64.8%)  bare local var -- origin needs dataflow\n     45 (19.1%)  strings/bytes.NewReader -- NO CROSSING AT ALL\n     11 ( 4.7%)  os.Stdin      11 (4.7%) net.Conn     1 http body\n     15 ( 6.4%)  other expression\n\ngo.yaml declares bufio.{NewScanner,NewReader} as ipc_recv unconditionally, with\nthe note \"When wrapping os.Stdin\" -- a condition no catalogue row can enforce.\nipc_recv is in AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, so it mints untrusted_input. Therefore\n`bufio.NewScanner(strings.NewReader(s))` invents an untrusted-input taint SOURCE\nout of a string literal, at 19.1% of the measured population.\n\nThat is the same defect class as INV-nular F6 (adjacency is not a crossing) and\n0006's family A (classified by NAME, not by what it does) -- the family the\nevidence names as the largest single cause of low precision. So the first\ndeliverable here DELETES false sources; the os.Stdin/net.Conn inference that\nadds true ones is the second.\n\nSEQUENCING UNCHANGED. The item's own \"BEFORE BUILDING\" step still stands and is\nnow the first thing to do: measure what fraction of the 153 undecidable sites\nthe existing dataflow actually resolves, and publish that number before any\ndesign is chosen. If it is low, this item is much bigger than it looks.\n\nINV-zumin's ruling also still stands and is not touched by the band ruling: do\nNOT close INV-bagok by emitting BOTH boundaries. One answer per call site plus\nan honest abstention."  # 6b30
